            <h2 id="manufacturing-process">Manufacturing Process Overview (End-to-End)</h2>

            <p>Manufacturing personal care aerosols is a controlled industrial process governed by safety standards and
                quality systems. Unlike non-pressurized cosmetics, aerosol manufacturing introduces risks related to
                pressure, flammability, and gas handling, requiring specialized infrastructure.</p>

            <p>From bulk compounding to final packing, each step must be validated to ensure consistency and compliance.
            </p>

            <h3>Bulk Compounding Philosophy</h3>
            <p>Bulk preparation focuses on achieving homogeneity, stability, and compatibility—not just mixing
                ingredients. Temperature control, agitation method, and contamination prevention are critical,
                particularly for fragrance-containing systems.</p>

            <h3>Aerosol Filling Line Configuration</h3>
            <p>Aerosol filling lines are purpose-built systems designed to handle liquids and propellants safely. Line
                configuration depends on can size, propellant type, and target production volume. Automation level
                directly impacts consistency and labor safety.</p>

            <h3>Crimping, Gassing, and Leak Testing</h3>
            <p>Crimping secures the valve to the can, while gassing introduces the propellant under controlled
                conditions. Leak testing is mandatory to ensure container integrity and prevent hazardous failures
                during storage or transport.</p>

            <h3>Stability, Compatibility, and Shelf-Life Considerations</h3>
            <p>Finished products undergo stability and compatibility testing to verify that pressure, spray performance,
                and chemical integrity remain within specifications over time.</p>

            <h3>Manufacturing stages typically include:</h3>
            <table>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Bulk liquid preparation</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Can filling and valve crimping</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Propellant charging</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Water bath or pressure-based leak testing</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>Final inspection and packing</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>

